# Half-Life snark. Measured by vrcardgen, finished by hand.
#
# Part J: "Take one from the nest on the chest. It squirms in the hand and
# bites if held too long. Throw it, or drop it at your feet and let it hunt."
#
# There is nothing to work and nothing to load. A snark is released, and
# after that it has opinions of its own - so the card carries no fuse,
# because what happens next is the creature's and not a timer's.
#
# The squirming and the biting are Part I and Part G: a thing in the hand
# with its own behaviour, and haptics to match. Neither belongs in a card.

weapon v_squeak
match  bones 67  seqs 6  hash 0x7a41a0d2

# The bone every position in this card is measured in - the controls, the
# grab points, the chamber, the ejection port. Nothing recorded it until
# the engine had to place a control in the world to ask whether a thumb is
# near it; the simulator never needed one, because it never works in world
# space. Taken from the generator, which has always called this bone the
# WEAPON BODY and is what measured these numbers in the first place.
body   "R_Arm_bone"

type   thrown
fuse   0           # it is alive; it decides
